;; The multi-session cockpit's data source — as DATA (PLAN-027 M1, FUP-036).
;;
;; This is the producer of `data/sessions`, the cross-session overview the
;; cockpit layout projects into a grid of cards. It USED to be Elixir
;; (`SpellAgent.Tui.Cockpit.sessions/1`) — the body naming the feature. Now it
;; is a frozen PTC program the mind authored, registered via
;; `data-source/register` and run on the query clock through the read-only
;; `DataSource.Tools` tier (`tool/session-registry/lineage`,
;; `tool/hist/trace-summary`).
;;
;; The UNION lives here, in data: for each live session (its lineage row), attach
;; its bounded content summary. The body provides only the two read-only
;; primitives; the SHAPE of the join — what a cockpit row is — is this program.
;;
;; `SpellAgent.Tui.Cockpit.install/0` reads this file, freezes the program, and
;; registers it as the `sessions` source. A missing/malformed file falls back to
;; the compiled Elixir producer (never-brick — the body keeps a floor).

;; BOUND the grid (review Sβ P2): take at most 12 sessions BEFORE tracing each
;; — the old Elixir Cockpit.sessions/1 capped at @max_sessions before decorating.
;; session-registry/lineage has no cap, so without `take` a reproject would call
;; hist/trace-summary for every live session and build an unbounded card set.
(data-source/register
  {:name "sessions"
   :program
   (quote
     (map
       (fn [s]
         (merge s (tool/hist/trace-summary {:id (get s "id")})))
       (take 12 (tool/session-registry/lineage))))})
